\end{document}
```

This will produce:

Accuracy = $\frac{Correct\ predictions}{Total\ predictions}$

If you want to include actual numbers, you can replace `Correct predictions` and `Total predictions` with the desired values. For example:

```
\documentclass{article}
\begin{document}

$$Accuracy = \frac{100}{120} = 0.83$$

\end{document}
```

This will produce:

Accuracy = $\frac{100}{120} = 0.83$

Note that you can use the `siunitx` package to format the numbers with the correct units, for example:

```
\documentclass{article}
\usepackage{siunitx}
